00:32:57.780 --> 00:33:03.280
Like, you know, better than putting Coca-Cola on the scoreboard, right?

00:33:03.380 --> 00:33:05.180
Like that feels like forced advertising.

00:33:05.360 --> 00:33:10.620
At least this is like, oh, from the makers of baseball simulator, it's Kung Fu Heroes.

00:33:10.960 --> 00:33:13.540
You didn't like going to KFC and Crazy Taxi?

00:33:13.720 --> 00:33:18.840
I didn't like driving my car exclusively with Valvoline either.

00:33:21.440 --> 00:33:23.180
They're no longer a sponsor of the show.

00:33:23.320 --> 00:33:28.260
Never were actually. Well, I mean, now we can't say that they were after what happened.

00:33:28.460 --> 00:33:35.300
And we can't say if baseball simulator 1000 is on the essential games list or not until

00:33:35.780 --> 00:33:36.940
we do that segment.

00:33:36.960 --> 00:33:40.640
So what do you say we do it right now on the essential games list?

00:33:43.260 --> 00:33:48.860
All right. So, you know, I gave that whole speech about how I feel about playing NES baseball games.

00:33:49.020 --> 00:33:51.360
You can kind of imagine where the vote's going to go here.

00:33:51.360 --> 00:33:57.440
But I'll start by saying that baseball simulator 1000 surprised me because I thought this was

00:33:57.440 --> 00:34:03.080
just going to be a very like technical game where gameplay was almost put second.

00:34:03.080 --> 00:34:07.720
And it was more about, you know, like really thinking about the statistics and building the

00:34:07.720 --> 00:34:12.240
team and being the manager and other like fun things could work off of that.

00:34:12.240 --> 00:34:18.580
But instead, it is a game that is mostly about the baseball at these long games that you're

00:34:18.580 --> 00:34:22.260
going to play for as many as 165 games in a single season.

00:34:22.560 --> 00:34:28.200
And then like, yeah, what you do kind of influences the statistics and build out that, you know,

00:34:28.320 --> 00:34:29.880
like the team grows from there.

00:34:30.020 --> 00:34:31.200
So that's cool and all.

00:34:31.200 --> 00:34:37.280
Like I actually feel like for an NES baseball game where you're mostly going to want to be

00:34:37.280 --> 00:34:38.300
playing baseball.

00:34:38.480 --> 00:34:42.980
This isn't out of the park baseball where you're mostly going to be like adjusting your lineups

00:34:42.980 --> 00:34:47.940
and making sure that your pitchers aren't tired and stuff like that and having a full featured

00:34:47.940 --> 00:34:51.800
rotation and trading players like that's what those simulator games are for.

00:34:51.900 --> 00:34:55.440
But this is really like baseball simulator junior, right?

00:34:55.440 --> 00:35:01.840
Like it's giving you just what you need to feel like you're doing more than just playing

00:35:01.840 --> 00:35:06.520
games of baseball on pre-assigned teams and you just happen to pick the most op team.

00:35:06.640 --> 00:35:09.760
Like, no, you can build your team and see where it takes you.

00:35:09.880 --> 00:35:16.660
But mostly you're playing 165 games of baseball or just five or maybe just one exhibition game

00:35:16.660 --> 00:35:17.920
and realizing it's not for you.

00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:21.140
And I'm not I don't fall into that last category.

00:35:21.140 --> 00:35:27.120
I played more than one, but I still don't feel like baseball simulator is taking baseball

00:35:27.120 --> 00:35:29.360
up a level even on the NES.

00:35:29.640 --> 00:35:31.980
So no, not on the essential games list for me.

00:35:32.300 --> 00:35:38.560
Joe. Yeah, it's really cool to me that the level of simulation and I say that it's cool to me

00:35:38.560 --> 00:35:39.420
knowing this.

00:35:39.540 --> 00:35:46.660
It's not for me personally, but it's cool that like someone who really is into baseball can

00:35:46.660 --> 00:35:50.980
make their little league team if they know all their statistics and play through a game.

00:35:50.980 --> 00:35:53.300
Like that's that's a great feature.

00:35:54.240 --> 00:35:56.900
And, you know, like you said that they didn't just go that route.

00:35:57.060 --> 00:36:01.280
They also went the route of like, hey, if you just want to have fun and like mess around,

00:36:01.900 --> 00:36:08.260
here's this ultra these ultra league that like you can, yeah, become a tornado or you can do

00:36:08.260 --> 00:36:12.640
all this like crazy goofy stuff while playing it to really give it a little extra life.

00:36:12.640 --> 00:36:19.580
But it does definitely does not like tip the scales of a baseball game or a sports game

00:36:19.580 --> 00:36:24.420
on the NES that like to that extreme high quality.

00:36:24.640 --> 00:36:28.360
We always talk about what you would need out of something like this to put it on the essential

00:36:28.360 --> 00:36:32.360
games list. So for me, I'm also not going to vote it essential.

00:36:33.080 --> 00:36:42.480
Sean. I would I would describe this not so much as baseball simulator junior, but more baseball

00:36:42.480 --> 00:36:50.420
sandbox because it calling it a simulator is kind of disingenuous, I think, because of how

00:36:50.420 --> 00:36:51.800
wacky things can get.

00:36:51.800 --> 00:36:56.860
But I also really like the concept of this game.

00:36:57.060 --> 00:37:01.080
I like what it brought to 2D baseball.

00:37:02.540 --> 00:37:14.100
I think that I still prefer baseball stars just because it seemed more what you were kind

00:37:14.100 --> 00:37:19.420
of making your own felt a bit more not realistic, but.

00:37:20.120 --> 00:37:28.120
Uh. Not as much like just plugging numbers in like you kind of grew attached to your characters,

00:37:28.120 --> 00:37:35.340
whereas in this one, you're just sort of making a simulacrum of whatever you whatever you want

00:37:35.340 --> 00:37:37.180
that there's there's less constraints.

00:37:37.460 --> 00:37:41.060
So I think that this is still really fun.

00:37:41.240 --> 00:37:47.800
I think there's a lot of especially in like the arcade aspects and the the goofy powers and

00:37:48.680 --> 00:37:51.200
making an earthquake or making a field or blow up.

00:37:51.280 --> 00:37:55.520
Those are really cool. But I'm also going to not put this on the essential games list.

00:37:55.860 --> 00:37:58.440
Sean, you bring up a great point there at the end about the difference between it and

00:37:58.440 --> 00:38:05.800
baseball stars. It's like baseball stars is the baseball RPG, you know, like because even the stats that

00:38:05.800 --> 00:38:08.300
you're editing in that one aren't statistics, right?

00:38:08.380 --> 00:38:13.860
Like you're assigning actual like attributes like you would in a RPG.

00:38:13.860 --> 00:38:16.500
So I I like that it does differentiate them.

00:38:17.000 --> 00:38:19.260
You know, I would have to go back and play baseball stars.

00:38:19.440 --> 00:38:25.440
I do remember that being more exciting even from a gameplay point of view, like if the

00:38:25.440 --> 00:38:28.760
action felt really good and yet the fielding was still responsive.

00:38:29.640 --> 00:38:31.940
So I'm not sure, you know, where I would land on that.

00:38:32.040 --> 00:38:35.760
But all said, competent baseball game we've got here, which is not something you could say

00:38:35.760 --> 00:38:37.720
every time you play an NES baseball game.

00:38:37.880 --> 00:38:41.740
That's true. You know, it's funny.

